      "comment": "Traupman’s word, a diminutive of his <span lang=\"la\">melodrāma</span> for opera (p. 354), from Greek; no ancient author has either. The sung solos of Roman comedy were <span lang=\"la\">cantica</span> (Cic. Fam. 9.22.1; Liv. 7.2.9), so a Roman would have called a musical a play with many <span lang=\"la\">cantica</span>."
